# ORION CTL µ-ROS Libraries

Welcome to the libraries for the ORION actuators and control with µ-ROS adaptation.

## Content

Here you can find the next elements:

- **[constants](/orion_base/orion_ctl_micro_ros/lib/constants/constants.hpp):** Related with PID and PWM values for constants.
- **[encoder](/orion_base/orion_ctl_micro_ros/lib/encoder/):** Oriented to create encoder objects to use two-channel encoders of DC motors to get speed and direction.
- **[hardware](/orion_base/orion_ctl_micro_ros/lib/hardware/hardware.hpp):** Related with the ports value of the actuators.
- **[motor](/orion_base/orion_ctl_micro_ros/lib/motor/):** For using a DC Motor with a L298N driver having access to control the direction and the speed of the motor.
- **[pid](/orion_base/orion_ctl_micro_ros/lib/pid/):** Controller implementation to compute the motor movement.
- **[servo](/orion_base/orion_ctl_micro_ros/lib/servo/):** For using a ServoMotor, in this case, a MG996r to set/get the motor position on rad and degrees.

## Troubleshooting

### Robot moving in opposite direction

Review the port connection or exchange the ports in the [Hardware Constants File](/orion_base/orion_ctl_micro_ros/lib/hardware/hardware.hpp)

### µ-ROS not compiling

Ensure you have properly followed the instructions to compile µ-ROS code with PlatformIO. Check [micro_ros_platformio](https://github.com/micro-ROS/micro_ros_platformio)

## Library Structure

Each library lives in its own subdirectory and is compiled by PlatformIO as a
static library linked into the firmware image.

```plaintext
lib/
├── constants/
│   └── constants.hpp       ← PID gains, PWM limits, control rate
├── encoder/
│   ├── encoder.hpp
│   └── encoder.cpp         ← Quadrature decoder (speed + direction)
├── hardware/
│   └── hardware.hpp        ← GPIO pin definitions (motors, encoders, servos)
├── motor/
│   ├── motor.hpp
│   └── motor.cpp           ← L298N DC motor driver (direction + PWM speed)
├── pid/
│   ├── pid.hpp
│   └── pid.cpp             ← Discrete PID controller for wheel velocity
├── servo/
│   ├── servo.hpp
│   └── servo.cpp           ← MG996R servo (position in radians / degrees)
└── README                  ← this file
```

The firmware entry point (`src/main.cpp`) includes these headers directly;
PlatformIO's Library Dependency Finder resolves them automatically.
